# ==============================================================================
# Servex Contractor Environment Variables Template (Client-Side Mobile App)
# ==============================================================================
# IMPORTANT SECURITY NOTE:
# Only public configuration variables prefixed with EXPO_PUBLIC_* may reside here.
# Private secrets (API keys, auth tokens, service role keys) must NEVER be configured
# with EXPO_PUBLIC_* as Expo bundler inlines them directly into public client builds.
# ==============================================================================

# 1. Google OAuth 2.0 Client ID (Web Application Client ID from Google Cloud Console)
# Redirect URI authorized in Google Cloud: https://auth.expo.io/@nikhil9209/servex-contractor
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-google-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com

# 2. Supabase Cloud Backend (Public Client URL & Anon Public API Key)
# Project URL & Anon Public Key from Supabase Dashboard > Project Settings > API
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-supabase-project.supabase.co
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-supabase-anon-key

# ==============================================================================
# SERVER-SIDE ONLY CONFIGURATION (DO NOT PLACE IN CLIENT .env)
# ==============================================================================
# Live SMS Gateway Provider credentials (Fast2SMS for India, Twilio for Global)
# run behind a secure server-side boundary in the Supabase Edge Function (`send-otp-sms`).
# Set these secrets securely via Supabase CLI or Supabase Dashboard:
#
#   supabase secrets set FAST2SMS_API_KEY=your-fast2sms-api-key
#   supabase secrets set TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=your-twilio-sid
#   supabase secrets set TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=your-twilio-auth-token
#   supabase secrets set TWILIO_PHONE_NUMBER=your-twilio-phone
#
# DO NOT add EXPO_PUBLIC_ prefixes to these credentials.
# ==============================================================================
